	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046466936?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Agri metaverse Intelligence is an advanced online predictive model that is grounded on machine learning algorithms and advanced statistical models to predict the prices of 22 agricultural commodities. The system produces the correct five-year forecasts (2025-2029) based on past price data (2014-2024) and external economic factors and environmental factors. It is a decision support application using the Streamlit framework, a variety of time series models, including ensemble models, ARIMA, SARIMAX, and Prophet, to improve the quality and strength of forecasts and minimize financial risks to strategic agricultural economic planning through quantitative and evidence-based forecasting. It is a user-friendly, beginner easily to understand and dashboard allowing the stakeholders, which are agricultural traders, government policymakers, farmer cooperatives, and financial institutions, to access accurate and data-driven forecasts to predict commodity prices and evaluate financial risks. © 2026 IEEE.},
